# Ekostay Platform — repository-root ignores.
#
# Each entry below is here because committing it would be HARD TO UNDO. Git history
# is permanent in any practical sense: a secret or a PII file removed in a later
# commit is still in the history, still clonable, and still has to be treated as
# leaked. So these are excluded before the first commit, not after.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- credentials
# accounts/.env holds the Zoho Analytics client_secret and refresh_token.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ------------------------------------------------------------- Deluge exports
# accounts/deluge/Accounts.ds line 22851 is a LIVE hardcoded DoubleTick API key.
# Rotate it before this is ever reconsidered. F_B.ds is excluded for consistency,
# though it carries no credential of its own — it does carry
# `void DeleteAllRecords()` at line 4645, which wipes 14 tables.
*.ds

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- the PII
# Vendor_Master.csv — 8,063 real vendors: PANs, GST registrations, phone numbers,
# free-text bank details. The other master-data exports are tracked; these two are
# categorically different and stay out.
master-data/Vendor_Master.csv*
**/master-data/Vendor_Master.csv*
**/master-data/*.csv.orig.csv

# All_Employee_Masters.csv — 475 real employees with Name, DOB, Email and Phone.
# Caught by inspecting the staged file list rather than by the pattern above, which
# only looked for the vendor file. Worth remembering that "is it PII?" has to be
# asked per file, not per pattern.
**/master-data/All_Employee_Masters.csv

# The same two exports arrive from Creator under their REPORT names, with a
# download counter in parentheses. Added 29-Aug-2026 after 'All Vendor Masters (6).csv'
# — 8,156 real vendors — landed untracked but perfectly committable, because the
# patterns above only matched the renamed copies. Match the source names too.
**/master-data/All Vendor Masters*.csv
# And the FORM export, whose name uses a space rather than an underscore:
# 'Vendor Master.csv'. Third near-miss on this one file — the pattern has to
# match every name Creator and a human can produce, not just the canonical one.
**/master-data/Vendor Master*.csv

# Transactional exports, added 31-Aug-2026. Not PANs or bank details, but 11,205
# real orders naming vendors, villas and GUEST STAY DATES (Checked In / Check Out).
# Business data plus an occupancy record — not source, and regenerable from Creator.
**/master-data/All Vendor Order Bookings*.csv
**/master-data/All Raw Material Requests*.csv
**/master-data/All Expenses*.csv
**/master-data/All Bookings*.csv

# Blanket rule for master-data, added 31-Aug-2026 after the FOURTH near-miss.
# Naming each export by hand kept failing — the file arrives under whatever Creator
# called the report, and three of four new exports slipped through. Invert the
# default: ignore every CSV/JSON here, then re-allow the two small F&B masters that
# are genuinely safe to track. A new export is private until someone decides
# otherwise, which is the right way round for a folder holding production data.
**/master-data/*.csv
**/master-data/*.json
!**/master-data/All Item Masters.csv
!**/master-data/UOM Report.csv
!**/master-data/_index.json
**/master-data/All Employee Masters*.csv

# ------------------------------------------------- exported production data
# ~251 MB of real payments, expense legs and vendors pulled from Zoho Analytics.
# Regenerable with `php artisan zoho:inspect <view>`; not source.
storage/app/zoho/
**/storage/app/zoho/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ PHP / Laravel
/accounts/vendor/
/accounts/node_modules/
/accounts/public/build/
/accounts/public/hot
/accounts/public/storage
/accounts/storage/*.key
/accounts/storage/pail
/accounts/.phpunit.cache
/accounts/.phpunit.result.cache
/accounts/bootstrap/cache/*.php

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------- node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------ local
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log

# Screenshots dropped for reference are working material, not source. The
# directory itself is tracked via its .gitkeep.
/accounts/docs/screenshots/*
!/accounts/docs/screenshots/.gitkeep

# ------------------------------------------------------- live Creator session
# .auth/creator.json is a LIVE Zoho session: full read AND write access to the
# production Creator cluster. Same class of secret as a refresh token. Deleted
# after each screenshot run; ignored so it can never be committed even briefly.
.auth/
**/.auth/

# Screenshots of the running app and of live Creator. accounts/.gitignore already
# excludes accounts/docs/screenshots/*, but fnb/ has its own now, and a rendered
# screen carries whatever data was on it — live-app.png shows real vendors and
# villas. Working material, not source.
**/docs/screenshots/*.png
**/docs/screenshots/*.jpg
